//? Title: Regularized Regression: Shrinkage and Exact Zeros
//? Subtitle: Match the penalty convention before comparing coefficients
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An unpenalised fit can use large unstable coefficients or retain weak predictors. We compare
ridge, lasso and elastic-net proximal updates on an orthogonal design with a closed-form optimum.
A fixed penalty path makes shrinkage and exact threshold zeros visible without claiming a
validation-selected penalty.
)
\toc

> The method

With nonnegative mask m (zero for an unpenalised intercept), the objective is

$$
J(w)=\frac{\|Xw-y\|^2}{2N}+\lambda_1\sum_j m_j|w_j|+
\frac{\lambda_2}{2}\sum_j m_jw_j^2,\quad
w_j^*=\frac{\mathrm{sign}(a_j)\max(|a_j|-\lambda_1,0)}{1+\lambda_2}
\quad(X^TX/N=I,m_j=1).
$$
\alttext(Elastic net adds weighted absolute and squared penalties. On orthogonal penalised columns its solution soft-thresholds each least-squares coefficient then divides by one plus the ridge penalty.)

For the smooth part, g=Xᵀ(Xw-y)/N+lambda2 m*w. A step first forms z=w-rate*g and then
soft-thresholds z by rate*lambda1*m. A sufficiently small step (at most the reciprocal smooth
Lipschitz constant) gives descent. Lasso's proximal step produces exact zeros; taking an ordinary
gradient of |w| generally does not. Penalty strength depends on loss normalisation and predictor
scales. The visible loop uses tensor SGD for the smooth objective, then applies the L1 proximal map
under NoGradGuard. copy_ preserves the learnable leaf captured by the optimizer; rebinding w
would leave that optimizer attached to the old tensor. Adam with the same scalar threshold
would not implement this Euclidean proximal-SGD objective.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/regularized_regression_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/regularized_regression_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/regularized_regression_concept.tikz > build/regularized_regression_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/regularized_regression_concept.svg build/regularized_regression_concept.dvi > build/regularized_regression_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/regularized_regression_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
