> Conclusion

The orthogonal solution explains both ridge shrinkage and lasso zeros under the exact loss
normalisation used here. The fixed penalty path verifies implementation rather than choosing a
model. Correlated predictors and training-only scaling require separate validation and KKT checks.

> References

- [Parikh and Boyd (2014), Proximal Algorithms](https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/papers/prox_algs.html).
